al comic foil to a man with his  head firmly up his own ass and to the  society he has created shrek is the ugly  green reality check duloc desperately  needs whenever he encounters an  unnecessarily complex system or  highfalutin attitude his blunt approach  to life brings it crashing down where  there is a stifling order he deflates it  with humor or creative disorder i'm an  agent of chaos to kick the movie off  shrek literally wipes his ass with a  book of fairy tales  later he blatantly ignores social norms  which the human citizens of duloc follow  even when they believe their lives are  in immediate danger his no-nonsense  approach to fiona's rescue highlights  the obvious flaws in the princesses and  by proxy the audience's understanding of  heroism you're meant to charge in sword  drawn better fight  that's what all the other knights did  yeah right before they burst on the  flame even his speech patterns undercut  the pompous and fake medieval dialogue  used by characters caught up in their  own delusional stories wait mr knight  this be at our first meeting should it  not be a wonderful  romantic moment yeah  sorry lady  just by being himself shrek points out  the absurdities of people like farquaad  and places like dulon he simplifies and  loosens up things that have gotten over  complicated and inflexible at the same  time he complicates ideas the rest of  the world takes for granted most  importantly in standing up for himself  and ogres in general he calls into  question the idea that there can be a  simple binary division between good and  bad beauty and ugliness perfection and  imperfection he explains this to donkey  in one of the film's most iconic scenes  onions have layers ogres have layers  onions have layers  you get it we both have layers and later  man ain't none but a bunch of little  dots  you know donkey sometimes things are  more than they appear and in spite of  shrek sarcasm and for all the film's  reputation as a smart alecky postmode